1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,800
Um... maybe...

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,700
I should take a shower first.

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:14,300
Getting cold feet after coming this far?

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,300
That's not...

5
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,800
You're trying to act calm and cool,

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,500
but I can tell.

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,700
You can tell what?

8
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,290
Why not just say...

9
00:00:33,290 --> 00:00:35,200
it's your first time?

10
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:38,650
That's not...

11
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:41,200
true.

12
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,500
Are you… sure?

13
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:55,940
<i>Timing and subtitles brought to you by</i>

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:01,770
<i>My heart's racing.  </i>

15
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:04,000
<i>Is this love?</i>

16
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:15,620
<i>[Ai-Chan's Secret | Episode 1]</i>

17
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:33,210
Go Ai!

18
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:41,100
Hey, Reo! What was that?

19
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:43,600
You got sloppy at the end, Aiko.

20
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:45,600
Just because you're a little taller than me?

21
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:49,100
It's more about skill level than height.

22
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,900
Let's go another round!

23
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:54,300
Come on, let's go. Let's go.

24
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:57,500
I'm not gonna lose next time!

25
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:01,880
You sure keep fighting after losing, every time.

26
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:04,000
If I beat him,

27
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,070
I'll be the best player in the basketball club.

28
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:11,330
You two sure are great rivals, huh?

29
00:02:11,330 --> 00:02:14,190
That's because Reo is my enemy.

30
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,290
<i>[AIKO KASUMI: an energetic, competitive, basketball-loving high school girl]</i>

31
00:02:17,290 --> 00:02:20,420
You're totally messing around with that Aiko Kasumi, right?

32
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:21,950
Well, she's funny.

33
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:24,080
She gets worked up so quickly and then challenges me to a game.

34
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:27,590
<i>[REO AMANO: the most popular guy at Kafuu High School and the ace of the basketball club]</i>

35
00:02:27,590 --> 00:02:30,370
So you really do enjoy it, after all.

36
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,570
<i>[KENJI KUBO: Reo's best friend and basketball teammate since middle school]</i>

37
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:35,740
Well, she <i>is</i> my toy.

38
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:39,140
Next time, I'm, definitely, not going to lose!

39
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:42,200
<i>[Kasumi]</i>

40
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,920
Yum! Meat is the best!
<i>[RANJI KASUMI: the easily-flattered third son, often swayed by his girlfriend]</i>

41
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:51,510
Aiko, you jerk...

42
00:02:51,510 --> 00:02:55,380
That meat was mine! Aiko!

43
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:59,000
Pipe down!

44
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,710
Crap. I'm going to be sick.

45
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:04,860
Your meat is my meat, and my meat is my meat!

46
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:08,410
- Aiko!
- What, what?

47
00:03:08,410 --> 00:03:09,750
Wait, Aiko!

48
00:03:09,750 --> 00:03:13,460
Drank too much, Ritsuki?

49
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,110
My meat!
<i>[MAKOTO KASUMI: first son and parental substitute when the parents are gone]</i>

50
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:18,400
That's too much meat talk for one morning.

51
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:23,700
- Oh, right. Dad and Mom said they're in Paris now.
- Really?

52
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:27,200
Makoto, stop eating and catch her!

53
00:03:27,990 --> 00:03:29,680
Here you go. Have a good day!

54
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:34,040
- Thank you, dear brother!
- Aiko, this isn't over—

55
00:03:34,790 --> 00:03:38,200
Victory is mine. See you later!

56
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:44,540
Ranji, isn't it time you stop bickering so wildly with our little sister?

57
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:47,880
She's never acted like a little sister!

58
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,980
<i>[Kafuu High School]</i>

59
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:54,800
Wait, wait, wait!

60
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,240
What do you want so early in the morning?

61
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:59,270
Let's go another round, Reo.

62
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:01,960
I won't lose today!

63
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,200
- What is it?
- Well...

64
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:08,580
- Thanks for the morning chuckle.
- Huh?

65
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:11,450
Is that a yes or no?

66
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:13,670
I accept your challenge.

67
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,750
Yes!

68
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:17,750
<i>[Kafuu High School]</i>

69
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:34,750
I lost.

70
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,180
I win.

71
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:43,680
- Ai!
- She's so cool!

72
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:47,120
Ai, I'll always be devoted to you!
<i>[ERENA YAMAGUCHI: the leader of Ai's groupies]</i>

73
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:50,510
I appreciate it. I may lose the games,

74
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:54,030
but when it comes to number of fans, I win.

75
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:57,450
One, two...

76
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:02,000
Eight?!

77
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,230
Seven!

78
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:08,480
So I win?

79
00:05:12,930 --> 00:05:16,890
That jerk! With his smug little face...

80
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:20,320
Reo's super popular.

81
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,110
Everyone's got lovey-dovey eyes for him.

82
00:05:23,110 --> 00:05:26,100
He's just a tiny bit better than me at basketball!

83
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:31,070
Yeah. And he's handsome and gets great grades.

84
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:36,650
I hate it. He's so perfect, it makes me sick!

85
00:05:36,650 --> 00:05:39,440
You haven't changed a bit since third grade, Ai.

86
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:42,220
Even though everyone is nuts about boyfriends and having sex...

87
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:45,290
you're all, "Basketball! Game! God damn it!"

88
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:48,060
It's endearing, but I do worry.

89
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:50,590
<i>[HIROKO KITAUCHI: Ai's best friend since childhood. Very understanding.]</i>

90
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:54,730
What? Worry? About what?

91
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:58,490
You're a high school girl that knows nothing about love.

92
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:00,530
I don't care about that!

93
00:06:00,530 --> 00:06:04,400
Basketball is a hundred times more fun than love!

94
00:06:06,770 --> 00:06:08,650
What are you doing?!

95
00:06:08,650 --> 00:06:12,250
The wind of love is 100 times sweeter!

96
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:18,410
Love sweeps through our entire body. It makes you feel like your heart is about to stop.

97
00:06:18,410 --> 00:06:22,540
What's wrong, Hiroko? You're acting weird today.

98
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:26,570
I'm about to be bowled over by a gust of wind.

99
00:06:26,570 --> 00:06:29,590
Does that mean you're...?

100
00:06:29,610 --> 00:06:32,430
- In love.
- In love?!

101
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:35,690
Will you help me?

102
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:40,980
If that's the case, just leave it to me!

103
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:42,050
<i>[Maid Cafe | Spica]</i>

104
00:06:42,050 --> 00:06:45,090
I'm sorry. I don't think I can do this.

105
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:49,070
Three of the girls quit all at once, so it's been hard.

106
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:52,960
Didn't you know that Ritsuki's been having trouble?

107
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,980
He's just reaping what he's sown.

108
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:59,950
But if I'm seen wearing this, my life is over!

109
00:06:59,950 --> 00:07:03,690
Yeah, it's over. My cafe is over, too!

110
00:07:03,690 --> 00:07:07,270
<i>[RITSUKI KASUMI: Second son, manager of the maid cafe, lady-killer playboy]</i>

111
00:07:07,270 --> 00:07:10,980
Turning someone with no sex appeal to anyone into a maid...

112
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:14,080
Hey, Ritsuki! I can hear everything you say.

113
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:17,750
Don't you think that's rude to say to your little sister?

114
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:21,490
Oh, sorry! So you're my little sister, huh? Not brother?

115
00:07:21,490 --> 00:07:27,640
Screw him. I hope this cafe goes under, and he becomes homeless forever.

116
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,910
Come on now, both of you.

117
00:07:30,790 --> 00:07:32,730
What's so great about Ritsuki, anyway?

118
00:07:32,730 --> 00:07:36,900
He's the most perverted, idiotic loser of all my brothers!

119
00:07:36,910 --> 00:07:39,010
That's kind of cute about him.

120
00:07:39,010 --> 00:07:42,230
It's like you can't leave him on his own.

121
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:44,300
No way.

122
00:07:53,350 --> 00:07:55,140
No way.

123
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:58,260
Ritsuki!

124
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:21,880
What's up with this place? There's no one here.

125
00:08:26,780 --> 00:08:28,960
Welcome home, Master.

126
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:32,330
- I'm very sorry, we're still getting ready—
- There's a sign outside, ain't there?!

127
00:08:32,330 --> 00:08:34,650
"Post-Refurbishment Reopening," it says.

128
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:38,970
I told you, I'm not being a maid!

129
00:08:38,970 --> 00:08:41,530
- So you're going to lose this game?
- Huh?

130
00:08:41,530 --> 00:08:44,750
This is a battleground between men and women.

131
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:46,790
Who will seize the initiative?

132
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:50,040
How much can you enthrall the guy?

133
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:53,520
If you forfeit the game and run away, you lose.

134
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:56,090
I lose?

135
00:08:56,710 --> 00:09:00,960
This is your weapon. Might be too difficult for you, though.

136
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:06,230
So please, Master, if you'd wait a little longer...

137
00:09:06,230 --> 00:09:08,560
I've had enough of this!

138
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,920
Master! What's the matter?

139
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,960
You're so cute!

140
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:19,850
Master! You're leaving already?

141
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:21,850
I'd like an extension!

142
00:09:21,850 --> 00:09:24,490
Thank you very much!

143
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:28,810
I hope you'll eat lots and regain your strength!

144
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:33,550
- One of everything!
- Yay!

145
00:09:33,550 --> 00:09:36,340
Thank you very much!

146
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:41,390
Cocoa drink, full of energy... Shoot!

147
00:09:41,390 --> 00:09:43,830
- It's a goal, a goal!
- A goal!

148
00:09:43,830 --> 00:09:45,130
- Enjoy!
- Thank you!

149
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:47,190
She's got a knack for it.

150
00:09:49,150 --> 00:09:52,060
But you're cuter, Hiroko.

151
00:09:52,690 --> 00:09:54,700
No way.

152
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,350
Have a good night!

153
00:09:58,350 --> 00:10:00,740
- See you!
- Please come again!

154
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:03,390
I'll be waiting!

155
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:09,440
This might actually be really fun!

156
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:12,790
Welcome!

157
00:10:14,290 --> 00:10:18,060
No way!

158
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:20,080
Welcome home!

159
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:23,840
- Huh? Kitauchi?
- That's right.
<i>[DAICHI &amp; RYOTA: 2nd year students at Kafuu High, members of the basketball club]</i>

160
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:25,330
- You work here?
- I do.

161
00:10:25,330 --> 00:10:27,240
You're such a cute maid!

162
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:29,440
What are you guys doing here all together?

163
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:33,620
- We got a coupon from over there.
- I see! Well, I'll show you to a seat.

164
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:36,440
Over there. Three meters. Straight ahead.

165
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:40,030
Right, right. Over there.

166
00:10:40,030 --> 00:10:43,340
Come on, I'll show you!

167
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:47,280
So? What do you want to eat? Pick from here.

168
00:10:47,280 --> 00:10:49,840
Hey...

169
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:55,410
I'm sorry!

170
00:10:55,410 --> 00:10:58,500
- I'm really sorry!
- It's okay.

171
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:00,860
What do I do? It's not coming out!

172
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:03,170
- Hey...
- I apologize!

173
00:11:03,170 --> 00:11:07,980
I'll pay for the dry cleaning!

174
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,100
You're...

175
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:19,690
cute.

176
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,550
Don't worry about the cleaning.

177
00:11:27,550 --> 00:11:29,620
Tell me your name.

178
00:11:33,870 --> 00:11:36,170
I'm Reo Amano.

179
00:11:36,170 --> 00:11:37,960
What's your name?

180
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:43,060
My name...

181
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:45,850
Mai Toda? Who's that?

182
00:11:45,850 --> 00:11:50,210
It's my grandma's name. Mai Toda.

183
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:52,790
- Oh! The one that rode around on that huge motorcycle?
- Yeah.

184
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:57,540
Reo was totally enthralled by the college student Mai Toda.

185
00:11:59,250 --> 00:12:02,400
He had no idea it was me.

186
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:04,220
Look.

187
00:12:04,230 --> 00:12:07,650
<i>[Mai, please go on a date with me.]</i>

188
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:10,420
No one realized it was you.

189
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:12,610
Right?

190
00:12:12,610 --> 00:12:15,670
And Reo invited me out!

191
00:12:15,670 --> 00:12:21,090
- As soon as he falls in love with me, ta-da!
- No, no!

192
00:12:21,090 --> 00:12:23,790
And so I'll be counting on you!

193
00:12:23,790 --> 00:12:25,030
Huh? Counting on me for what?

194
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:29,680
You'll lend me some super cute clothes, right?

195
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:32,720
<i>Sure, I guess that's fine.</i>

196
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:37,150
<i>Reo's a guy, though. If things turn serious, he might do something rash.</i>

197
00:12:38,050 --> 00:12:42,300
<i>Bring it on! If he takes it seriously, I win.</i>

198
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:45,770
<i>Then the game ends.</i>

199
00:13:11,950 --> 00:13:13,870
It's so pretty.

200
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:28,410
This is an amazing little hidden place!

201
00:13:28,410 --> 00:13:31,200
I came here a lot with my family as a kid.

202
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:34,850
- The sunset is really pretty here.
- The sand feels great!

203
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:43,960
Are you listening to what I'm saying?

204
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:49,860
Come on! Get over here, Reo!

205
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:16,750
♫ <i>Just wanna, wanna, wanna, wanna go and take it</i> ♫

206
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:25,250
♫ <i>Just wanna, wanna, wanna, wanna go and take it</i> ♫

207
00:14:26,770 --> 00:14:31,050
♫ <i>You are so free</i> ♫

208
00:14:31,050 --> 00:14:35,500
♫ <i>You are suspicion</i> ♫

209
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:40,450
♫ <i>Been a lonely, lonely, lonely, lonely only</i> ♫

210
00:14:40,450 --> 00:14:44,730
♫ <i>Lonely, lonely, lonely, lonely only</i> ♫

211
00:14:44,730 --> 00:14:49,240
♫ <i>Lonely, lonely, lonely, lonely only</i> ♫

212
00:14:57,040 --> 00:15:00,600
I wish we had brought some swimsuits.

213
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:03,290
The water's too cold for swimming now.

214
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:10,440
I'd be fine!

215
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:18,000
I see something! It's a tiny fish!

216
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,450
I'm sorry.

217
00:15:25,450 --> 00:15:27,640
Are you okay?

218
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:31,840
Are you just dizzy?

219
00:15:32,850 --> 00:15:36,880
Or are you trying to tempt me?

220
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:38,320
What?

221
00:15:42,050 --> 00:15:46,310
Oh! No, that's not...

222
00:15:55,070 --> 00:15:57,840
Let's head back.

223
00:15:57,840 --> 00:16:00,610
I'll buy you a change of clothes from somewhere.

224
00:16:00,610 --> 00:16:02,190
Okay.

225
00:16:05,970 --> 00:16:08,960
What? There are no more busses?

226
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,880
That's a little early!

227
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:13,620
The last bus just left.

228
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:16,520
We can take a taxi to the train station...

229
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:19,120
but will one drive by?

230
00:16:19,130 --> 00:16:21,180
Why don't we walk?

231
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:24,080
The last train will be gone by the time we get there.

232
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:27,590
That's true.

233
00:16:28,450 --> 00:16:31,480
But we'll catch a cold if we stay outdoors like this...

234
00:16:34,990 --> 00:16:37,460
<i>[Love Hotel]</i>

235
00:16:38,650 --> 00:16:41,420
Should we go...

236
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:43,490
take a rest?

237
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:51,240
That's fine.

238
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,010
Let's...

239
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:58,510
stay the night.

240
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:14,350
So this is a love hotel...

241
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:20,690
Mai.

242
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:25,400
Thank you.

243
00:17:44,090 --> 00:17:46,700
Are you nervous?

244
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:50,530
No, I'm not.

245
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:53,200
I see.

246
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:57,910
You're...

247
00:17:57,910 --> 00:18:00,350
used to this, aren't you?

248
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:05,750
You come to places like this a lot?

249
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:11,250
Would you like to find out?

250
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:13,890
What?

251
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:19,990
Mai...

252
00:18:23,230 --> 00:18:26,660
Um... maybe...

253
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:29,570
I should take a shower first.

254
00:18:29,570 --> 00:18:33,150
Getting cold feet after coming this far?

255
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:35,330
That's not...

256
00:18:36,510 --> 00:18:38,650
You're trying to act calm and cool,

257
00:18:39,410 --> 00:18:41,530
but I can tell.

258
00:18:43,730 --> 00:18:45,650
You can tell what?

259
00:18:49,110 --> 00:18:51,350
Why not just say…

260
00:18:51,350 --> 00:18:53,380
it's your first time?

261
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:58,140
That's not...

262
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:00,770
true.

263
00:19:02,550 --> 00:19:05,320
Are you...

264
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,060
sure?

265
00:19:24,090 --> 00:19:25,710
I'm sorry...

266
00:19:27,090 --> 00:19:29,590
for making you nervous.

267
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:32,870
I wasn't that nervous…

268
00:19:32,870 --> 00:19:36,120
You've been making my heart go nuts,

269
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:39,120
so I just wanted to change it up and make your heart beat faster.

270
00:19:41,170 --> 00:19:43,360
What do you mean?

271
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:48,720
You don't know?

272
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:53,830
Anyway,

273
00:19:54,650 --> 00:19:58,210
I don't want things with you to be half-hearted, Mai.

274
00:20:00,550 --> 00:20:03,230
They have bathrobes,

275
00:20:03,230 --> 00:20:05,370
so I'll go change first.

276
00:20:12,910 --> 00:20:14,920
A hotel?!

277
00:20:21,610 --> 00:20:26,140
<i>[I'm staying the night in a hotel with Reo... Please be my alibi!]</i>

278
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,890
<i>I'm good for your alibi.</i>

279
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:33,400
<i>But don't rush into anything, okay?</i>

280
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:39,250
I'm sorry. Were you waiting?

281
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,920
You look totally different from usual.

282
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:44,870
- Really?
- Yeah.

283
00:20:52,390 --> 00:20:55,190
I'll sleep on the sofa.

284
00:20:55,190 --> 00:20:57,390
You use the bed.

285
00:20:58,290 --> 00:21:00,960
No, that's way too small for you.

286
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:03,800
The bed is so big, we can both sleep there.

287
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:06,140
I can't do that.

288
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:09,440
I'm really holding myself back,

289
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:12,950
but I don't know what could happen in the bed.

290
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:21,510
We'll just... sleep quietly tonight.

291
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:36,810
Good night.

292
00:22:51,870 --> 00:22:54,670
♫ <i>What awaits in this battle of love?</i> ♫

293
00:22:54,670 --> 00:22:57,630
♫ <i>It seems it won't end in a draw</i> ♫

294
00:22:57,630 --> 00:23:00,610
♫ <i>You hated loosing,</i> ♫

295
00:23:00,610 --> 00:23:04,710
♫ <i>So I won't let you go easy on me</i> ♫

296
00:23:07,350 --> 00:23:08,950
Mai...

297
00:23:09,850 --> 00:23:11,550
are you okay?

298
00:23:14,390 --> 00:23:15,950
Yeah.

299
00:23:15,950 --> 00:23:17,980
♫ <i>I don't wish for anyone to know my secret</i> ♫

300
00:23:17,980 --> 00:23:20,940
♫ <i>I want to steal you away</i> ♫

301
00:23:20,940 --> 00:23:25,720
♫ <i>The secret that belongs to only us. 1on1</i> ♫

302
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:31,680
♫ <i>I make you acting like a kid with just a sweet kiss</i> ♫

303
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:36,110
♫ <i>Only I know this</i> ♫

304
00:23:36,110 --> 00:23:38,710
<i>This is a game.</i>

305
00:23:38,710 --> 00:23:41,480
♫ <i>Rather than touching each other, we can melt
into one another's embrace</i> ♫

306
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:44,490
<i>A game I can either win or lose.</i>

307
00:23:44,490 --> 00:23:47,900
♫ <i>I'll let you get near just to return you like a wave</i> ♫

308
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:49,430
Well...

309
00:23:49,430 --> 00:23:51,270
♫ <i>I'll steal you away before anyone gets the chance</i> ♫

310
00:23:51,270 --> 00:23:53,320
I'm really embarrassed,

311
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:56,240
so, let me come out and say it like this.

312
00:24:03,430 --> 00:24:05,090
Please,

313
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,490
let's start dating, for real.

314
00:24:09,450 --> 00:24:16,360
<i>Timing and subtitles brought to you by</i>

315
00:24:17,530 --> 00:24:19,740
<i>So, this...</i>

316
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:25,390
<i>isn't love. Definitely not.</i>

317
00:24:25,390 --> 00:24:26,980
<i>[Next time]
He's acting like nothing happened. </i>

318
00:24:26,980 --> 00:24:28,270
<i>Then lock Aiko away!</i>

319
00:24:28,270 --> 00:24:29,670
<i>That's love!</i>

320
00:24:29,670 --> 00:24:32,200
<i>You've got to be kidding me. Someone like Reo?</i>

321
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,580
<i>You don't sit around and wait for destiny, you reach out and grab it.</i>

322
00:24:34,580 --> 00:24:36,380
<i>I wasn't serious about it!</i>

323
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:40,160
<i>You said you lost, but you really won from the start.
[This drama is a work of fiction]</i>
